  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PSE 2 - &quot;WATA&quot;: INTERPOL Supported Regional Maritime Policing (I-SRMP)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The objective of the PSED is to &quot;strengthen the capabilities of maritime law enforcement agencies in the Gulf of Guinea to tackle maritime-based crime more effectively through deeper investigations into the wider organizational structures of organized criminal groups and reinforced security at port facilities&quot;. 

In line with the above, the PSED will thus focus on improving beneficiary units&#x2019; abilities to manage a crime scene and debrief kidnap victims, strengthen security measures at key port facilities, as well as to investigate the link between maritime-enabled transnational organized crime and terrorism.

The PSED will focus on Gulf of Guinea maritime security institutions and countries, particularly those within Zones E and F, including Benin, C&#xf4;te d&#x2019;Ivoire, Ghana, Nigeria and Togo.</narrative>
  </description>
